      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The anti-anginal effect of the ACE inhibitor enalapril, at a dosage of 5 mg twice a day, was tested in a randomised, placebo-controlled double-blind trial on 12 normotensive patients with proven coronary-heart disease. There was a reduction of exercise-induced ST depression by 22% already after the first dose of 5 mg. After 15 days of treatment the ST depression had decreased by 35% (P less than 0.05)."},
